WEBVTT

NOTE Payments sync, 2026-11-20. Fake meeting for Serra's evals: every person and company is invented.

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.500
<v Mei>Can everyone hear me? I think Tomás is still
<v Mei>joining from the train.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Robin>I can hear you. Morning all. Did anyone watch the match last night?

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.000
<v Priya>Only the second half. Terrible refereeing. Okay, let's start, we have a lot.

4
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:20.000
<v Priya>First topic is webhook retries. Right now deliveries retry with backoff for 72 hours and merchants say it's too long, they get
<v Priya>stale events days later.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:28.000
<v Mei>We looked at the numbers. Ninety-four percent of deliveries that succeed at all succeed within the first three attempts. After that it's mostly dead endpoints.

6
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.000
<v Tomás>Sorry, I'm here now. Train wifi. What did I miss?

7
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Robin>Webhook retries. Mei has numbers.

8
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:44.000
<v Mei>My proposal: three attempts and then we dead-letter it. Merchants can replay from the dead-letter queue in the dashboard.

9
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.000
<v Robin>Yes, let's do that. Three attempts, then dead-letter. Tomás, does that work for the worker?

10
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.000
<v Tomás>It's a config change mostly. I can update the retry config by Thursday the 27th.

11
00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:00.000
<v Priya>How long do we keep things in the dead-letter queue? Some merchants only look at the dashboard once a week.

12
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Mei>Seven days?

13
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:12.000
<v Robin>Make it fourteen. Dead-lettered events are kept for 14 days, then deleted. A week is too short for small merchants.

14
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Mei>Fine by me, fourteen days.

15
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.000
<v Priya>Should we email merchants when something lands in the dead-letter queue? I don't know if that's helpful or just noise.

16
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.000
<v Robin>Let's not decide that today. Priya, can you ask two or three merchants?

17
00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Priya>Sure. I'll also write the customer note about the retry change.

18
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:38.000
<v Tomás>One more thing while we're on payments-api. I saw a PR last week where payments-api wrote to the ledger tables directly.

19
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Robin>That can't happen. payments-api never calls the ledger directly. It always goes through the ledger service. Everyone agree?

20
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.000
<v Mei>Agreed.

21
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Tomás>Agreed, I'll leave a comment on that PR.

22
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:56.000
<v Priya>Okay. Quick round, anything else? No? Then the rest is status, I'll post it in the channel. Thanks all.

23
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.000
<v Mei>Bye! Enjoy the weekend.
